{"full":"hf:OpenGVLab/ControlLLM","spaceId":"OpenGVLab/ControlLLM","name":"ControlLLM","source":"huggingface","description":"An interactive AI application on Hugging Face Spaces.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","topics":["gradio","region:us"],"technologies":["Python"],"likes":10,"created":"2023-12-15T10:44:40.000Z","updated":"2024-08-23T08:15:58.000Z","license":"apache-2.0","runtime":"SLEEPING","appUrl":"https://opengvlab-controlllm.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/OpenGVLab/ControlLLM","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T13:40:48.721Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T13:40:48.721Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T13:40:48.721Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🚀","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["ControlLLM: Augmenting Large Language Models with Tools by Searching on Graphs [Paper]","We present ControlLLM, a novel framework that enables large language models (LLMs) to utilize multi-modal tools for solving complex real-world tasks. Despite the remarkable performance of LLMs, they still struggle with tool invocation due to ambiguous user prompts, inaccurate tool selection and parameterization, and inefficient tool scheduling. To overcome these challenges, our framework comprises three key components: (1) a $\\textit{task decomposer}$ that breaks down a complex task into clear subtasks with well-defined inputs and outputs; (2) a $\\textit{Thoughts-on-Graph (ToG) paradigm}$…"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/OpenGVLab/ControlLLM/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e83ea7afffc5d10d05568ccef9c0f99a932510589e76faab500d1a77250f7c45","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T14:46:13.541Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T13:40:48.760Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"ControlLLM: Augmenting Large Language Models with Tools by Searching on Graphs [Paper]","sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/OpenGVLab/ControlLLM/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"require